msgid "NPC_BARD"
msgstr "Bard"

msgid "DLG_OLD_DRUNK_1"
msgstr "You look like people who have buried someone. Sit. And do not look at my cup: it has been empty since the day I stopped hearing them laugh. I was rich, you know? Powerful. I had a name, lands and a house full of children."

msgid "DLG_OLD_DRUNK_2"
msgstr "Lucifer came on a rainy night to collect a debt I signed drunk, years before, without reading. He did not want the gold. He wanted the souls: my wife, my children, even the dog. He tore them out one by one, in front of me, and locked them in a storm of glass. I was left with the bodies. Cold, in their beds, eyes still open."

msgid "DLG_OLD_DRUNK_3"
msgstr "The bottle is down here, in the cellar of the Necromancer: the king's alchemist, forgotten in the dark to guard the gold, who sold his soul to the devil and now stitches the dead to serve him. He sleeps on the treasure the founders of Tortuga hid, and on the bones of the whole kingdom that lost the war."

msgid "DLG_OLD_DRUNK_4"
msgstr "The people here poisoned and burned the rats down there. But the Necromancer stitched them back together, one by one, and now they serve dead. Earth and rot run in his veins, and earth fears fire. Bring fire."

msgid "DLG_OLD_DRUNK_5"
msgstr "Keep all the gold: gold does not laugh, does not call for its father, does not scream at dawn. I only want the bottle. Bring it and I will pay everything I have left, to hear them laugh one more time… or at least to hear them rest."

msgid "DLG_OLD_DRUNK_ACTIVE"
msgstr "The manhole is on Main Street. Fire, I said. Fire! And the bottle: a storm of screams trapped in glass. Bring it to me before the silence of the house takes me too."

msgid "DLG_OLD_DRUNK_DONE"
msgstr "I… I hear them. They laugh. And then they fall silent, at last, at peace. Thank you. Take what I promised and buy me a drink: the first in years that is not to forget."

msgid "DLG_KEEPER_1"
msgstr "Sit down, rest. In Tortuga nobody asks where the gold comes from — only whether it pays."

msgid "DLG_BARD_QUEEN_1"
msgstr "The Necromancer was once the king's alchemist: left in the dark to guard the gold, he sold his soul and began to stitch the dead."

msgid "DLG_BARD_QUEEN_2"
msgstr "Now earth and rot run in his veins, and earth fears fire — remember the song."

msgid "DLG_BARD_1"
msgstr "Every monster was something else once. Come back and I'll sing you its story."

