msgid "NPC_ELF_ARCHER"
msgstr "Explorer"

msgid "DLG_ARCHER_1"
msgstr "Good day, travelers. Mind your step: these trails are full of very old things, and of things that used to be people. I am an explorer, and I roam the world after rarities for my collection. I have a shelf made only of teeth."

msgid "DLG_ARCHER_2"
msgstr "For months I have been after the dinosaur bone dagger. They say the Stone Golem King, who sleeps in the temple in the east of the forest, carries it driven into his chest, and that the stone around the blade bleeds."

msgid "DLG_ARCHER_3"
msgstr "Wake the temple, bring down the King and tear the dagger from his chest for me. In return I will hand over one of the two keys to the gate of the Leshy's lair, deep in the forest."

msgid "DLG_ARCHER_ACTIVE"
msgstr "The temple lies at the far east of the woods, where the soil is dark from so much blood. Touch its stones to wake the King. The dagger is unmistakable, curved and white, the length of a forearm. Bring it and the key is yours."

msgid "DLG_ARCHER_DONE"
msgstr "Magnificent! There is still dried blood on the hilt. This blade will shine in my collection. The key is yours, as agreed. Keep it safe: together with Aelindra's, it opens the gate to the Leshy's lair. Talk to the warden before it."

msgid "QUEST_FOREST_LESHY"
msgstr "The Bone Dagger"

msgid "QUEST_FOREST_LESHY_DESC"
msgstr "The Explorer wants the dinosaur bone dagger for her collection of horrors. The Stone Golem King keeps it driven into his chest, in the temple in the east of the forest. Wake the temple, defeat the King, pull out the dagger and hand it over: in return she gives one of the two keys to the gate of the Leshy's lair."

msgid "DLG_HUNTER_1"
msgstr "Strangers! Mind the hedge when you leave — the grove is not what it was. I'm Bertram. Elara and I are all that's left of Ferncroft."

msgid "DLG_HUNTER_2"
msgstr "Something crawls out of the dark in the grove: lean, green, all claws. Three of them took my last deer and the rest of my patience."

msgid "DLG_HUNTER_3"
msgstr "Clear them out and I'll pay what I can. They're Earth-blooded things — they hate Fire."

msgid "DLG_HUNTER_ACTIVE"
msgstr "Three of them, in the grove, past the stones. Fire, remember. Fire."

msgid "DLG_HUNTER_DONE"
msgstr "Quiet at last! The deer are coming back. If you want more, talk to the Hermit and the Keeper in the squares."

msgid "DLG_WIFE_1"
msgstr "Don't mind the smell, it's the hides. I'm Elara. Bertram says you fight what hunters cannot."

msgid "DLG_WIFE_2"
msgstr "Stones have started to walk in these woods, trampling where our paths used to be. My racks, my fish… everything. The ones who know how to wake and tame such things are the Hermit of the Stone and the elf Aelindra, Keeper of the Pyre, who walks the trail."

msgid "DLG_WIFE_3"
msgstr "Talk to them — and come back in one piece. The things inside the caves — toads, bats, reptiles and beasts — are no joke either."

msgid "DLG_WIFE_ACTIVE"
msgstr "Stone and fire sleep in the squares — talk to the Hermit and the Keeper. The ice one is to the east."

msgid "DLG_WIFE_DONE"
msgstr "The woods are breathing again. Ferncroft thanks you — take what we saved."

msgid "QUEST_FOREST_REPTILES"
msgstr "Lurkers in the Grove"

msgid "QUEST_FOREST_REPTILES_DESC"
msgstr "Bertram the Hunter asks you to clear the pack of Forest Reptiles from the grove. They are Earth — they fear Fire."

msgid "QUEST_FOREST_GOLEMS"
msgstr "Walking Stones"

msgid "QUEST_FOREST_GOLEMS_DESC"
msgstr "Elara the Tanner asks you to defeat the Stone, Ice and Fire Golems of the Forest: the stone and fire ones sleep in the squares and only wake when the Hermit and the Keeper call them."

msgid "PROP_VILLAGE_SIGN"
msgstr "Ferncroft"

msgid "PROP_VILLAGE_SIGN_TEXT"
msgstr "Ferncroft — half a dozen houses, one hunter and one tanner. Strangers welcome."

msgid "HUD_QUEST_PLAIN"
msgstr "Quest: {quest}"

msgid "PROP_COIN_BAG"
msgstr "Coin bag"

msgid "ARENA_MINE"
msgstr "Crystal Mine"

msgid "PROP_TO_MINE"
msgstr "Path to the Mine"

msgid "MONSTER_CRYSTAL_GOLEM"
msgstr "Crystal Golem"

msgid "ARENA_DOCKS"
msgstr "Docks"

msgid "PROP_TO_DOCKS"
msgstr "Gangway to the Docks"

msgid "PROP_TO_PORT"
msgstr "Back to the port"

msgid "MONSTER_CHITIN_BEAST"
msgstr "Chitinous Beast"

msgid "MONSTER_ANGLER"
msgstr "Anglerman"

msgid "MONSTER_STALKER"
msgstr "Stalker"

msgid "VALUABLE_HUMAN_HEART"
msgstr "Human Heart"

msgid "VALUABLE_ALTAR_BOOK"
msgstr "Altar Book"

msgid "VALUABLE_ALTAR_BOOK_DESC"
msgstr "Given by Ossael. The prayers of the drowned, written with their own fingernails: they make the altar in the center of the Sewer react. Bring the group to it and speak to the stone to wake the Impaled One. It cannot be sold or lost."

msgid "VALUABLE_CURSED_SKULL_DESC"
msgstr "Morvak's cursed skull, kept in the Fire Golem's chest. Hand it to the elf Aelindra, in the Forest, to purify the curse."

msgid "TOAST_QUEST_ITEM_KEEP"
msgstr "Quest item: it cannot be put in the stash."

msgid "VALUABLE_CURSED_SKULL"
msgstr "Morvak's Skull"

msgid "VALUABLE_OLD_SKULL"
msgstr "Old Skull"

msgid "QUEST_ROYAL_HEART"
msgstr "The Fallen King's Heart"

msgid "QUEST_ROYAL_HEART_DESC"
msgstr "The Capital's Priest wants to lay Veldmark's last king to rest. The Crypt Lord, in the Cemetery, keeps his heart: defeat him and bring the Human Heart to the Priest."

msgid "QUEST_ROYAL_SKULL"
msgstr "The Fallen King's Skull"

msgid "QUEST_ROYAL_SKULL_DESC"
msgstr "The Fort Commander carries the skull of Veldmark's last king. Defeat him and hand the Old Skull to the Priest."

msgid "DLG_PRIEST_HEART_1"
msgstr "You have walked the lands of Veldmark, haven't you? There, the last king of the defeated realm was dug up: Lucifer's demons took the body piece by piece."

msgid "DLG_PRIEST_HEART_2"
msgstr "I fought him in life, but no man deserves that. The Crypt Lord keeps his heart in the Cemetery. Bring me the heart and the Church pays in gold."

msgid "DLG_PRIEST_HEART_ACTIVE"
msgstr "Bring the Human Heart the Crypt Lord keeps in the Cemetery. When you have it, just hand it over."

msgid "DLG_PRIEST_SKULL_1"
msgstr "The heart and the lungs now rest. The skull is missing: the cursed Commander of the Fort carries it as a trophy for Lucifer."

msgid "DLG_PRIEST_SKULL_2"
msgstr "Bring the Old Skull and the king will have a whole grave. The Church pays well for it."

msgid "DLG_PRIEST_SKULL_ACTIVE"
msgstr "The Old Skull is with the Fort Commander. Hand it to me when you have it."

msgid "DLG_PRIEST_DONE"
msgstr "Veldmark's king rests, whole, thanks to you. May the light guide your steps, mercenaries."

msgid "DLG_SERVICE_TURN_IN"
msgstr "Hand over the relic"

msgid "TOAST_NEED_QUEST_ITEM"
msgstr "Missing: {item}"

msgid "MONSTER_FROG_KING"
msgstr "Impaled One"


msgid "MONSTER_RUIN_ALPHA"
msgstr "Pack Alpha"

msgid "MONSTER_SUCCUBUS_QUEEN"
msgstr "Succubus Queen"

msgid "MONSTER_TROLL_CHIEF"
msgstr "Troll Chief"

msgid "NPC_COURT_JESTER"
msgstr "Court Jester"

msgid "DLG_JESTER_1"
msgstr "Ah, the famous mercenaries of Tortuga! What an honor, what an honor…"

msgid "DLG_JESTER_2"
msgstr "(lowering his voice) Nobody pays attention to a fool — which is why I hear everything."

msgid "DLG_JESTER_3"
msgstr "The king's gold is vanishing from the vaults, and nobody in the castle notices. Come back when you're ready: I know where to look."

msgid "ARENA_BUNKER"
msgstr "Bunker"

msgid "PROP_TO_BUNKER"
msgstr "Bunker Hatch"

msgid "PROP_RETURN_FARM"
msgstr "Back to the Farm"

msgid "VALUABLE_WILD_MEAT"
msgstr "Wild Meat"

msgid "QUEST_ROYAL_BANQUET"
msgstr "The King's Banquet"

msgid "QUEST_ROYAL_BANQUET_DESC"
msgstr "The Court Jester wants meat on the king's table. The Pack Alpha, in the Ruins, has the best: defeat him and bring the Wild Meat to the Jester."

msgid "DLG_JESTER_BANQUET_1"
msgstr "Look at this table: apples, bananas… and not a piece of meat! The king is so distracted by the gold vanishing from the vaults that he forgot to eat like a king."

msgid "DLG_JESTER_BANQUET_2"
msgstr "The Pack Alpha, in the Ruins, has the most famous meat in the realm. Bring it and I will tell you what I know, fool to mercenary."

msgid "DLG_JESTER_BANQUET_ACTIVE"
msgstr "The Wild Meat is with the Pack Alpha, in the Ruins. The king's table is waiting, and so am I!"

msgid "DLG_JESTER_BANQUET_DONE"
msgstr "What a feast, what a feast! The king ate like never before. You have a friend in the castle."

msgid "NPC_RUINS_SPARTAN"
msgstr "Leonidas, the Veteran"

msgid "DLG_SPARTAN_1"
msgstr "Halt, strangers. I am Leonidas. I have held this entrance since the war brought down the walls, and nobody passes without telling me why."

msgid "DLG_SPARTAN_2"
msgstr "The goblins came after the fire, like rats after scraps. They roam in two packs: one in the eastern streets and one deep in the city, near the vault."

msgid "DLG_SPARTAN_3"
msgstr "They are quick and frail, but they come in numbers. They are creatures of the earth — Fire brings them down. Clear the streets and I will pay in gold."

msgid "DLG_SPARTAN_ACTIVE"
msgstr "The goblins still roam the streets: one pack to the east, another near the vault. Stay together and use Fire."

msgid "DLG_SPARTAN_DONE"
msgstr "Quiet in the streets for the first time in years. You have an old soldier's thanks. May the gods guard your shields."

msgid "QUEST_RUINS_GOBLINS"
msgstr "Goblin Plague"

msgid "QUEST_RUINS_GOBLINS_DESC"
msgstr "Leonidas, the Veteran, asks you to defeat the two goblin packs infesting the streets of the Ruins. They are Earth — they fear Fire."

msgid "PROP_BASKET"
msgstr "Basket"

msgid "NPC_FOREST_PYRE_KEEPER"
msgstr "Aelindra, Keeper of the Pyre"

msgid "DLG_PYRE_1"
msgstr "The pyre never dies, strangers. I am Aelindra, elf and warden of this Forest. I feed the fire with what the woods give back: bones, and what is left of them."

msgid "DLG_PYRE_2"
msgstr "Morvak the hunter flayed the animals here alive and nailed their hides to the trees. He died on his feet, headless, laughing. His skull does not burn: it whispers, and where the curse seeps, the bark of the trees bleeds."

msgid "DLG_PYRE_3"
msgstr "The Fire Golem keeps the skull inside his burning chest. Tear it out of him and bring it to me before the whisper reaches the roots. The embers are already stirring…"

msgid "TOAST_PYRE_AWAKENS"
msgstr "The embers roar: the Fire Golem awakens!"

msgid "PROP_MINIBOSS_CHEST"
msgstr "Mini-boss chest"

msgid "PROP_BOSS_CHEST"
msgstr "Boss chest"

msgid "TOAST_BOSS_CHEST"
msgstr "The boss left a chest!"

msgid "TOAST_MINIBOSS_CHEST"
msgstr "The mini-boss left a chest!"

msgid "MONSTER_DARK_ELF_LORD"
msgstr "Dark Elf Lord"

msgid "NPC_FORT_PENITENT"
msgstr "The Penitent"

msgid "DLG_PENITENT_1"
msgstr "I served the Queen of Succubi once. Now I kneel in this corridor and pay for it."

msgid "DLG_PENITENT_2"
msgstr "She sleeps in the hall beyond that arch, and she will not wake unless someone calls her by name. I know it."

msgid "DLG_PENITENT_3"
msgstr "Step back… I call her now. Fire is her blood: bring water, or bring luck."

msgid "TOAST_PENITENT_AWAKENS"
msgstr "The arch glows: the Succubus Queen awakens!"

msgid "NPC_FORT_EXILE"
msgstr "The Exile"

msgid "DLG_EXILE_1"
msgstr "They cast me out for questioning the Commander. I have waited in this corridor ever since."

msgid "DLG_EXILE_2"
msgstr "Beyond lies the Dark Elf Lord, captain of the crossbowmen. He keeps the south road and never lets anyone pass."

msgid "DLG_EXILE_3"
msgstr "Keep moving while he reloads, and let nothing get between you and the Commander's door. I will wake him for you."

msgid "TOAST_EXILE_AWAKENS"
msgstr "A horn sounds: the Dark Elf Lord awakens!"

msgid "QUEST_FOREST_FIRE"
msgstr "Morvak's Skull"

msgid "QUEST_FOREST_FIRE_DESC"
msgstr "The elf Aelindra, warden of the Forest and its animals, asks for the cursed skull of Morvak, the hunter who flayed the beasts of the woods and died laughing, headless. The Fire Golem keeps it in his burning chest: tear it out and bring it back before the curse rots the trees."

msgid "DLG_PYRE_ACTIVE"
msgstr "Bring Morvak's skull, strangers, before the curse reaches the trees. Listen: it still whispers the names of the animals he killed. The embers are already stirring… beware: the Fire Golem wakes when someone calls it."

msgid "DLG_PYRE_DONE"
msgstr "The skull screamed one last time and turned to ash. The animals sleep in peace again. Take what I owe you — and do not look back."

msgid "VALUABLE_HUMAN_LUNGS"
msgstr "Human Lungs"

msgid "QUEST_ROYAL_LUNGS"
msgstr "The Fallen King's Lungs"

msgid "QUEST_ROYAL_LUNGS_DESC"
msgstr "The Crypt Ogre, in the Cemetery, keeps the lungs of Veldmark's last king: defeat him and bring the Human Lungs to the Priest."

msgid "DLG_PRIEST_LUNGS_1"
msgstr "The heart now rests, but the king still does not breathe in peace: the lungs ended up with the Crypt Ogre, in the same Cemetery."

msgid "DLG_PRIEST_LUNGS_2"
msgstr "He is big and brutish, but only guards what he was told to. Bring the lungs and the Church pays again."

msgid "DLG_PRIEST_LUNGS_ACTIVE"
msgstr "The Human Lungs are with the Crypt Ogre, in the Cemetery. Hand them to me when you have them."

msgid "VALUABLE_ROYAL_SOUL"
msgstr "King's Soul"

msgid "QUEST_ROYAL_SOUL"
msgstr "The Fallen King's Soul"

msgid "QUEST_ROYAL_SOUL_DESC"
msgstr "The Tomb Guardian has trapped the soul of Veldmark's last king. Defeat him, in the Mine or the Cemetery, and bring the King's Soul to the Priest."

msgid "DLG_PRIEST_SOUL_1"
msgstr "The body is whole, but the king still does not rest: his soul, a little ghost that laughs at its own bad luck, was trapped by the Tomb Guardian."

msgid "DLG_PRIEST_SOUL_2"
msgstr "He wanders between the Mine and the Cemetery, where the statue wakes him. Bring the soul and the Church pays its last fee."

msgid "DLG_PRIEST_SOUL_ACTIVE"
msgstr "The King's Soul is with the Tomb Guardian, in the Mine or the Cemetery. Hand it to me when you have it."

msgid "ARENA_DESERT"
msgstr "Desert — Canyon"

msgid "PROP_TO_DESERT"
msgstr "Path to the Desert"

msgid "MONSTER_SAND_LAMASSU"
msgstr "Sand Lamassu"

msgid "MONSTER_QUEEN_SCORPION"
msgstr "Scorpion Queen"

msgid "NPC_SEATED_PIRATE"
msgstr "Pirate Captain"

msgid "DLG_PIRATE_1"
msgstr "Sit down, mercenary. See that pier out there, at the Docks? It used to be mine: now it's just frogs, bats and ugly anglerfish."

msgid "DLG_PIRATE_2"
msgstr "My ship docks there and I can't unload a barrel without losing a finger. Clear the pier for me."

msgid "DLG_PIRATE_3"
msgstr "Kill every critter on the Docks: frogs, ugly frogs, bats and the anglerfish. I pay in gold and rum… more in gold."

msgid "DLG_PIRATE_ACTIVE"
msgstr "There are still critters on the pier. Come back when the last one is floating."

msgid "DLG_PIRATE_DONE"
msgstr "The pier is clean! A toast to the mercenary who is not afraid to get their feet wet."

msgid "QUEST_DOCKS_SMUGGLERS"
msgstr "The Old Sea Wolf's Pier"

msgid "QUEST_DOCKS_SMUGGLERS_DESC"
msgstr "Pirate Captain wants Drowned Captain's Log, which Drowned Captain keeps at the bottom of the map. Get the books from the locals, wake the mini-bosses at the altar, trade their items for the keys, open the gate with the guardian and defeat Drowned Captain. Hand Drowned Captain's Log to Pirate Captain for a gold reward."

msgid "NPC_OLD_LADY"
msgstr "Tavern Old Lady"

msgid "DLG_OLD_LADY_1"
msgstr "Sit, sit. This old woman has seen many people walk through that door, and few return from the woods."

msgid "DLG_OLD_LADY_2"
msgstr "The Leshy lives in the Forest, a giant of bark and stone. He is Earth — Fire is what the old bark fears."

msgid "DLG_OLD_LADY_3"
msgstr "Bring him down and I will reward you. The ranger Aeliana waits on the trail."

msgid "DLG_OLD_LADY_ACTIVE"
msgstr "The Leshy sleeps deep in the woods. Take Fire with you, dears."

msgid "DLG_OLD_LADY_DONE"
msgstr "So the woods breathe again. How good to have you around."

msgid "NPC_SEWER_SCAVENGER"
msgstr "Ossael, the Skull Angel"

msgid "NPC_SEWER_RATCATCHER"
msgstr "Azazel, the Flaming Angel"

msgid "QUEST_SEWER_OLD_GATOR"
msgstr "The Bottle of Condemned Souls"

msgid "QUEST_SEWER_OLD_GATOR_DESC"
msgstr "Azazel wants the Bottle of Condemned Souls, which Lucifer sent him to fetch and the Horned Butcher stole: take the Grimoire of Embers to the scorched altar in the center of the sewer to call the demon, defeat him, and bring the bottle to Azazel to receive the spade key."

msgid "DLG_SEWER_GATOR_1"
msgstr "I have burned since the sky cast me out, and I burn deeper when Lucifer calls. He sent me to fetch the Bottle of Condemned Souls, the jewel of his cellar, and a butcher from hell itself stole it: the Horned Butcher, who carves souls with a cleaver and drinks them still warm. He fled to these sewers."

msgid "DLG_SEWER_GATOR_2"
msgstr "He does not leave his hideout on his own, and never walks alone: the Shadow Spirits of the souls he carved follow him, still screaming for the pieces they lost. He wears the bottle on his belt; I hear the souls inside at every step he takes."

msgid "DLG_SEWER_GATOR_3"
msgstr "Take this grimoire, written with my embers and my ash. Rest it on the scorched altar in the center of the sewer and read it aloud: it calls the Butcher by name. Bring him down and bring me the bottle; in return, the spade key I keep is yours."

msgid "DLG_SEWER_GATOR_ACTIVE"
msgstr "Still no bottle? Read the grimoire at the scorched altar in the center of the sewer and call the Butcher. Bring me the Bottle of Condemned Souls and let the fire, mine, do the rest."

msgid "DLG_SEWER_GATOR_DONE"
msgstr "The bottle… the souls sing inside, safe from his cleaver, for now. Lucifer will be pleased. Take the spade key: it is yours. I take the souls, and the ashes."

msgid "QUEST_SEWER_FROG_KING"
msgstr "The Bottle of Eternal Torment"

msgid "QUEST_SEWER_FROG_KING_DESC"
msgstr "Ossael, the Skull Angel, wants the Bottle of Eternal Torment, which the Impaled One tore from him along with his flesh: take the Altar Book to the altar in the center of the sewer, read the prayers of the drowned to wake the monster, defeat it and bring the bottle to Ossael to receive the heart key."

msgid "DLG_SEWER_FROG_1"
msgstr "These bones were once an angel, guardian of the drowned of this sewer, and I came to fetch the Bottle of Eternal Torment, where their suffering is kept so they can rest. I failed: a thing of flesh and planks tore off my flesh, my white feathers and the bottle, and nailed the souls of my drowned into its own wood. I hear each one scream inside each nail. Only bones and these black wings remain."

msgid "DLG_SEWER_FROG_2"
msgstr "Folks call it the Impaled One: it was assembled from bones and the planks of the walkways, nail by nail, and it drives its own spikes into whoever comes close. Every nail is a soul. It carries my bottle nailed to its chest and sleeps under the stone altar in the center of the sewer; it only wakes when someone reads the right book. Its weeping calls the other dead."

msgid "DLG_SEWER_FROG_3"
msgstr "Take the Altar Book, the prayers of the drowned, written with their own fingernails. Rest it on the stone and read it aloud. Bring the Impaled One down and bring me the Bottle of Eternal Torment; in return, the heart key I keep is yours."

msgid "DLG_SEWER_FROG_ACTIVE"
msgstr "Still no bottle? The Impaled One only wakes when the prayers are read at the altar in the center of the sewer. Every plank that falls frees a screaming soul… Bring me the Bottle of Eternal Torment, nailed to its chest."

msgid "DLG_SEWER_FROG_DONE"
msgstr "The bottle… their torment ends here, and the souls rise. Each one passed between my black wings before leaving, and I felt the cold of all of them. Thank you. Take the heart key: it is yours. I will stay on guard as long as there are drowned."

msgid "PROP_SEWER_SECTOR_1"
msgstr "Main Street Drains"

msgid "SIGN_SEWER_SECTOR_1"
msgstr "Sector 1 — Main Street Drains. Someone gnawed the grates from the inside. The toads here grew fat on what the city throws away… and on what it forgets."

msgid "PROP_SEWER_SECTOR_3"
msgstr "Bat Galleries"

msgid "SIGN_SEWER_SECTOR_3"
msgstr "Sector 3 — Bat Galleries. They sleep hanging from the ceiling's ribs and wake at the smell of meat. To the east, a flame that never dies: the post of an angel who burned."

msgid "PROP_SEWER_SECTOR_4"
msgstr "The War Dead's Pit"

msgid "SIGN_SEWER_SECTOR_4"
msgstr "Sector 4 — The War Dead's Pit. The defeated kingdom was thrown in here, living and dead together, and walled in. You can still hear the marching. To the east, a plaza scored by cleaver."

msgid "PROP_SEWER_SECTOR_5"
msgstr "Mushroom Chambers"

msgid "SIGN_SEWER_SECTOR_5"
msgstr "Sector 5 — Mushroom Chambers. What sprouts from these walls grows out of buried flesh. Beware the scorpions. The tunnel to the Necromancer's Chamber leaves to the south."

msgid "PROP_SEWER_NEST"
msgstr "The Necromancer's Chamber"

msgid "SIGN_SEWER_NEST"
msgstr "The Necromancer's Chamber. The fallen king's crown sways on a head that is not his. Souls are collected in glass here, and the war's gold serves as a bed. Come back equipped."

msgid "OPTIONS_QUEST_TRAIL"
msgstr "Quest objective footprints"

msgid "NPC_SEWER_FROG_ALTAR"
msgstr "The Impaled One's Altar"

msgid "DLG_FROG_ALTAR_1"
msgstr "A black stone altar, stained with sludge and worse things, in the heart of the sewer. There is a gap in the center, the size of a book, prayers of the drowned scratched into the stone with fingernails, and claw and nail marks around it."

msgid "DLG_FROG_ALTAR_2"
msgstr "You rest the Altar Book on the stone and read the prayers aloud: the floor trembles, the planks creak like bones and the Impaled One wakes in the altar room, the bottle nailed to its chest and a thousand nails weeping."

msgid "TOAST_FROG_ALTAR_AWAKENS"
msgstr "The altar trembles: the Impaled One awakens!"

msgid "TOAST_BOOK_RECEIVED"
msgstr "Ossael handed over the Altar Book!"

msgid "DLG_FROG_ALTAR_LOCKED"
msgstr "The altar does not react. There is an empty gap in the middle of the stone, the size of a book. Ossael or Azazel must have what is missing."

msgid "MONSTER_TROLL_MAULER"
msgstr "Troll Mauler"

msgid "BEAST_TROLL_MAULER"
msgstr "Troll Mauler"

msgid "BEAST_TROLL_MAULER_LEGEND"
msgstr "A brute stooped under its own arms, with thick, scarred skin. It prowled the docks until the sewer became its home. They say it eats what the tide brings in, even what still moves."

msgid "BEAST_TROLL_MAULER_HINT"
msgstr "Slow and heavy: wait for the blow's warning and dodge. Fire hurts it more."

msgid "MONSTER_MUTANT"
msgstr "Mutant"

msgid "MONSTER_BARBARIAN_MONSTER"
msgstr "Barbarian Monster"

msgid "BEAST_BARBARIAN_MONSTER"
msgstr "Barbarian Monster"

msgid "BEAST_BARBARIAN_MONSTER_LEGEND"
msgstr "A horned orc warrior, cast out of his own band. He went down to the western canals and made them his territory, decorated with the skulls of those who came down uninvited."

msgid "BEAST_BARBARIAN_MONSTER_HINT"
msgstr "He hits fast and takes a lot: back off when his arm pulls back. Fire hurts him more."

msgid "MONSTER_CHAMP_WARRIOR"
msgstr "Mushroom Warrior"

msgid "BEAST_CHAMP_WARRIOR"
msgstr "Mushroom Warrior"

msgid "BEAST_CHAMP_WARRIOR_LEGEND"
msgstr "A mushroom warrior in armor, born of the flesh buried in the damp walls of the northwest. He guards the first canals with a sword that is a bone of the kingdom itself."

msgid "BEAST_CHAMP_WARRIOR_HINT"
msgstr "Agile with average health: dodge when he lifts the sword. Fire hurts him more."

msgid "MONSTER_CHEST_MIMIC"
msgstr "Mimic"

msgid "BEAST_CHEST_MIMIC"
msgstr "Mimic"

msgid "BEAST_CHEST_MIMIC_LEGEND"
msgstr "A chest that lost its lid and grew teeth. If you open it, it opens you: it swallowed the last mercenaries who wanted the Sewer's treasure, and they say you can still hear someone calling for help inside."

msgid "BEAST_CHEST_MIMIC_HINT"
msgstr "Fast and stubborn: running is no use. Fire burns it more."

msgid "PROP_SEWER_SECTOR_2"
msgstr "Canals of the Drowned"

msgid "SIGN_SEWER_SECTOR_2"
msgstr "Sector 2 — Canals of the Drowned. The water rises without rain and tastes of salt and blood. To the west, the plaza of planks; in the center of the map, a black stone waits for whoever can read the prayers of the dead."

msgid "MONSTER_SHADOW_SPIRIT"
msgstr "Shadow Spirit"

msgid "MONSTER_DEMON_TWELVE"
msgstr "Demon Twelve"

msgid "VALUABLE_BONE_DAGGER"
msgstr "Dinosaur Bone Dagger"

msgid "VALUABLE_KEY_SPADES"
msgstr "Key of Spades"

msgid "NPC_RESTAURANT_COOK"
msgstr "Head Cook"

msgid "DLG_COOK_1"
msgstr "Sit down, sit down! The roast just came out of the oven. Eat your fill: no traveler leaves my table hungry."

msgid "PROP_RESTAURANT"
msgstr "Restaurant"

msgid "PROP_RESTAURANT_TEXT"
msgstr "Capital Restaurant: a hot meal for those back from the battlefield."

msgid "VALUABLE_KEY_HEARTS"
msgstr "Key of Hearts"





msgid "PROP_RETURN_FOREST"
msgstr "Back to the Forest"


msgid "PROP_NEST_GATE"
msgstr "The Cellar Gate — it only opens with the Spade and Heart keys"

msgid "PROP_SEWER_KEY_SPADES"
msgstr "Key of Spades"

msgid "PROP_SEWER_KEY_HEARTS"
msgstr "Key of Hearts"

msgid "PROP_BOSS_GATE"
msgstr "Boss Gate"


msgid "TOAST_GATE_OPENED"
msgstr "The keys turn and the gate opens!"

msgid "TOAST_GATE_BOSS_ELEMENT"
msgstr "The final boss is {element}-element. Use {weak} to deal the most damage!"

msgid "NPC_FOREST_REPTILE"
msgstr "Gate Warden"

msgid "DLG_REPTILE_1"
msgstr "Ssss... stop, travelers. This gate is older than the forest. I have guarded it since before the bones that decorate the ground."

msgid "DLG_REPTILE_2"
msgstr "Behind it sleeps the Leshy, the giant of bark and stone, and his roots drink the dead. The gate falls only for those who bring TWO keys: Spades and Hearts. Both are held by the elves of the forest."

msgid "DLG_REPTILE_3"
msgstr "The Explorer and Aelindra, the Pyre Keeper, hold one each, but they ask a price: one wants a dagger made of dinosaur bone, torn from the chest of a stone king; the other, a cursed skull that still burns. Bring both keys to me and I will bring the gate down."

msgid "DLG_REPTILE_ACTIVE"
msgstr "I only open for both keys: Spades and Hearts, in the same bag. The elves have them: the Explorer and the Pyre Keeper. Bring them and the gate falls. Ssssmell that? It is the Leshy, hungry."

msgid "DLG_REPTILE_DONE"
msgstr "Both keys! Passss, the gate has fallen. Beware of what sleeps inside: it still sssavors the last ones who passed."

msgid "QUEST_FOREST_GATE"
msgstr "The Leshy's Gate"

msgid "QUEST_FOREST_GATE_DESC"
msgstr "The Gate Warden, a forest reptile, will only bring down the gate to the Leshy's lair for those who bring both keys, held by the elves: the Key of Spades (from the Explorer) and the Key of Hearts (from Aelindra, the Pyre Keeper). Hand both to him."

msgid "DLG_KEEPER_FOREST_1"
msgstr "Travelers and hunters go into the forest and never come back. The ones that do come back, come back later: their boots turn up on the road, with the feet still inside."

msgid "DLG_KEEPER_FOREST_2"
msgstr "They say the trees there have red roots. Beneath the ancient tree lies the gold of those who got lost, and the Leshy guards it. He made a pact with a demon and now makes whoever enters walk in circles until the flesh falls off the bone. And what Lucifer ordered hidden there is with him too."

msgid "DLG_KEEPER_FOREST_3"
msgstr "In my village the elders used to say: if the Leshy makes you walk in circles, turn your clothes inside out and light a fire. Forget the clothes. Bring the fire. He grows as tall as the trees… and trees burn. And if several of him appear, watch the shadow: the real one has his shadow on the right side."

msgid "DLG_KEEPER_FOREST_4"
msgstr "Among the hidden things is Adam's Rib, the first of all ribs, still warm, they say, as if just torn out. I do not want that bone in the demon's hands. There are two elves in the woods and a warden before the lair gate: talk to him first. Bring me the rib and I will pay well."

msgid "DLG_KEEPER_FOREST_ACTIVE"
msgstr "Still in one piece? Talk to the warden before the forest gate. When the Leshy falls, tear Adam's Rib out of him and bring it to me: the gold in the roots is yours."

msgid "QUEST_FOREST_TREASURE"
msgstr "Adam's Rib"

msgid "QUEST_FOREST_TREASURE_DESC"
msgstr "Travelers enter the forest and come back only in pieces. The Leshy, lord of the woods, made a pact with a demon, makes whoever enters walk in circles until they die, and buries in the roots of the ancient tree the gold of the dead and Adam's Rib, which Lucifer ordered hidden. He is Earth and fears Fire. The lair gate opens only through the warden, with the keys of the two elves. Defeat the Leshy and bring the rib to the Tavern Keeper."


msgid "RELIC_BRANCH_CROWN"
msgstr "Crown of Branches"

msgid "RELIC_BRANCH_CROWN_DESC"
msgstr "Twisted branches that sprouted from the Leshy's skull and still move. They smell of grave soil."

msgid "DLG_SERVICE_REST_TURN_IN"
msgstr "Rest / hand over the item"

msgid "TOAST_ITEM_RECEIVED"
msgstr "Received: {item}"

msgid "VALUABLE_ADAMS_RIB"
msgstr "Adam's Rib"

msgid "MONSTER_STONE_GOLEM_KING"
msgstr "Stone Golem King"

msgid "DLG_PYRE_WAIT"
msgstr "The dead of this wood scream too loudly for me to hear you. Speak first with the Explorer, who combs the temple in the east, and come back when the Stone King has fallen. Then I will listen."

msgid "DLG_TEMPLE_LOCKED"
msgstr "The temple stones are cold and silent. What sleeps beneath them has no reason to wake yet."

msgid "VALUABLE_SOULS_BOTTLE"
msgstr "Bottle of Condemned Souls"

msgid "VALUABLE_GATOR_BOOK"
msgstr "Grimoire of Embers"

msgid "VALUABLE_GATOR_BOOK_DESC"
msgstr "Given by Azazel, written with his embers and ash. Makes the altar in the center of the Sewer react: bring the group to it and speak to the stone to call the Horned Butcher. It cannot be sold or lost."

msgid "DLG_GATOR_ALTAR_2"
msgstr "You rest the Grimoire of Embers in the gap of the stone and read aloud: the stone burns your hand, the air reeks of sulfur and roasting flesh, and the Horned Butcher steps out of the embers, cleaver in hand, the souls screaming behind him."

msgid "TOAST_GATOR_ALTAR_AWAKENS"
msgstr "The altar boils: the Horned Butcher steps out of the embers!"

msgid "TOAST_GATOR_BOOK_RECEIVED"
msgstr "Azazel handed over the Grimoire of Embers!"

msgid "BEAST_HORNED_BUTCHER"
msgstr "Horned Butcher"

msgid "BEAST_HORNED_BUTCHER_LEGEND"
msgstr "A butcher from hell who fled to the sewer with the Bottle of Condemned Souls. He carves souls with a cleaver and drinks them still warm; their Shadow Spirits follow him, screaming for the pieces they lost."

msgid "BEAST_HORNED_BUTCHER_HINT"
msgstr "He charges head down: step aside when he roars and strike when his cleaver gets stuck. Water hurts him more."

msgid "BEAST_IMPALED_ONE"
msgstr "Impaled One"

msgid "BEAST_IMPALED_ONE_LEGEND"
msgstr "A monster of flesh, bone and walkway planks, nailed together: each nail traps the soul of a drowned person, who screams inside. It carries the Bottle of Eternal Torment nailed to its chest, sleeps under the altar in the center of the sewer and drives its own spikes into whoever comes close."

msgid "BEAST_IMPALED_ONE_HINT"
msgstr "It charges in a straight line: dodge the charge and strike when it stops, stuck fast. Old wood burns: fire hurts it more."

msgid "VALUABLE_TORMENT_BOTTLE"
msgstr "Bottle of Eternal Torment"

msgid "VALUABLE_STORM_BOTTLE"
msgstr "Bottle of the Soul Storm"

msgid "VALUABLE_SOULS_BOTTLE_DESC"
msgstr "Condemned souls screaming in chorus inside the glass. The jewel of Lucifer's cellar: Azazel wants it back before anyone opens it. It cannot be sold or lost."

msgid "VALUABLE_TORMENT_BOTTLE_DESC"
msgstr "The suffering of the drowned, held in glass and chains until someone frees it. Ossael seeks it: only then will the dead rest. It cannot be sold or lost."

msgid "VALUABLE_STORM_BOTTLE_DESC"
msgstr "A storm of souls trapped in glass: inside, a whole family laughs… and then screams. It is all the Old Drunk still wants. It cannot be sold or lost."

msgid "SHOP_POTIONS_MELIODAS"
msgstr "Meliodas, the Apothecary"

msgid "NPC_GATE_KEEPER"
msgstr "Gatekeeper"

msgid "DLG_GATE_KEEPER_WAIT_1"
msgstr "…Only those who bring me both keys may pass. Spades and hearts."

msgid "DLG_GATE_KEEPER_WAIT_2"
msgstr "Each of the sewer's mini-bosses guards one. Come back when you have both."

msgid "DLG_GATE_KEEPER_GIVE_1"
msgstr "…The keys. Yesss, those are the keys. It has been so long."

msgid "DLG_GATE_KEEPER_GIVE_2"
msgstr "The gate is yours. May the Rat Queen remember who guarded her."

msgid "DLG_GATE_KEEPER_DONE"
msgstr "The way is open. Do not look back."

msgid "HUD_BASIC_ATTACK"
msgstr "Attack"

msgid "HUD_POTION_SHORT_HEALTH"
msgstr "Health"

msgid "HUD_POTION_SHORT_RESOURCE"
msgstr "Mana"

msgid "HUD_POTION_SHORT_ELEMENTAL"
msgstr "Elem."

msgid "MONSTER_SPHINX"
msgstr "Sphinx"

msgid "NPC_DESERT_NOMAD"
msgstr "Sand Nomad"

msgid "NPC_DESERT_OASIS_KEEPER"
msgstr "Oasis Keeper"

msgid "NPC_DESERT_TEMPLE"
msgstr "Sun Temple"

msgid "NPC_DESERT_SENTINEL"
msgstr "Gate Sentinel"

msgid "VALUABLE_LAMASSU_HORN"
msgstr "Lamassu Horn"

msgid "VALUABLE_GOLDEN_SCARAB"
msgstr "Golden Scarab"

msgid "VALUABLE_KEY_CLUBS"
msgstr "Key of Clubs"

msgid "VALUABLE_KEY_DIAMONDS"
msgstr "Key of Diamonds"

msgid "TOAST_OASIS_AWAKENS"
msgstr "The oasis water stirs: the Scorpion Queen bursts from the sand!"

msgid "TOAST_SUN_TEMPLE_AWAKENS"
msgstr "The sun temple shakes: the Sand Lamassu awakens!"

msgid "QUEST_DESERT_HORN"
msgstr "The Lamassu's Horn"

msgid "QUEST_DESERT_HORN_DESC"
msgstr "The Sand Nomad wants the horn of the Lamassu, the stone guardian of the Sun Ruins to the east. Touch the temple, defeat the Lamassu and bring the horn: in return he gives one of the two keys to the Sphinx's gate."

msgid "QUEST_DESERT_SCARAB"
msgstr "The Golden Scarab"

msgid "QUEST_DESERT_SCARAB_DESC"
msgstr "The Oasis Keeper lost her people's golden scarab: the Scorpion Queen wears it on her stinger. Her words wake the Queen; bring back the scarab and receive the other key to the Sphinx's gate."

msgid "QUEST_DESERT_GATE"
msgstr "The Sphinx's Gate"

msgid "QUEST_DESERT_GATE_DESC"
msgstr "The Gate Sentinel only opens the way for those who bring both keys: Clubs (from the Nomad) and Diamonds (from the Oasis Keeper). Beyond the gate lies the Sphinx's Hall."

msgid "DLG_NOMAD_1"
msgstr "The sand swallows whole caravans, travelers. I am what is left of the last one: I know where every well and ruin lies, and what sleeps in each."

msgid "DLG_NOMAD_2"
msgstr "To the east, in the Sun Ruins, a temple guards the Sand Lamassu, a winged bull of stone. It carries a golden horn worth more than my whole caravan."

msgid "DLG_NOMAD_3"
msgstr "Touch the temple stones, bring down the Lamassu and bring me the horn. In return I give the Key of Clubs, one of the two that open the Sphinx's gate, north of the dunes."

msgid "DLG_NOMAD_ACTIVE"
msgstr "The temple is to the east: follow the road, cross the dunes and the quicksand. The horn is golden and as long as an arm. Bring it and the key is yours."

msgid "DLG_NOMAD_DONE"
msgstr "What a horn! With it I can rebuild my caravan. The Key of Clubs is yours; take it to the Gate Sentinel, together with the Diamonds one."

msgid "DLG_OASIS_1"
msgstr "Shh... the water listens. I have tended this oasis since before the sand arrived, and all that is left to me is this pool."

msgid "DLG_OASIS_2"
msgstr "The Scorpion Queen sleeps under the sand nearby, wearing my people's golden scarab on her stinger. Without it the oasis dries up for good."

msgid "DLG_OASIS_3"
msgstr "I will call her for you. Bring down the Queen and bring back the scarab: I will hand over the Key of Diamonds, the other one that opens the Sphinx's gate."

msgid "DLG_OASIS_ACTIVE"
msgstr "The scarab shines like a drop of sun. The Queen wears it on her stinger. Bring her down and bring it to me."

msgid "DLG_OASIS_DONE"
msgstr "The water sings again! The Key of Diamonds is yours. Take it to the Sentinel, in the lane north of the dunes."

msgid "DLG_OASIS_WAIT"
msgstr "Drink, rest. The water belongs to those who respect it."

msgid "DLG_SUNTEMPLE_1"
msgstr "The temple stones are warm, as if someone had just left. A roar of stone rises from below."

msgid "DLG_SUNTEMPLE_2"
msgstr "The Sand Lamassu awakens!"

msgid "DLG_SUNTEMPLE_LOCKED"
msgstr "An ancient temple buried in sand. Nothing answers your hands."

msgid "DLG_SENTINEL_1"
msgstr "Halt, strangers. This gate is older than the dunes, and behind it sleeps the Sphinx. I have watched it since the last king passed this way."

msgid "DLG_SENTINEL_2"
msgstr "The gate only falls for those who bring TWO keys: Clubs and Diamonds. The first is with the Sand Nomad at the camp; the second, with the Oasis Keeper."

msgid "DLG_SENTINEL_3"
msgstr "Both charge a price: a stone horn, a golden scarab. Bring both keys to me and I will open the way."

msgid "DLG_SENTINEL_ACTIVE"
msgstr "I only open with both keys, Clubs and Diamonds, in the same bag. The Nomad is at the camp; the Keeper, at the oasis west of the road."

msgid "DLG_SENTINEL_DONE"
msgstr "Both keys! The gate is open. Beware: the Sphinx asks a question and does not accept silence as an answer."

msgid "MONSTER_HULL_BEAST"
msgstr "Living Hull"

msgid "MONSTER_PORK_SHARK"
msgstr "Pork Shark"

msgid "MONSTER_DROWNED_CAPTAIN"
msgstr "Drowned Captain"

msgid "NPC_DOCK_MASTER"
msgstr "Harbor Master"

msgid "NPC_WRECKED_HULL"
msgstr "Beached Hull"

msgid "NPC_DOCK_FISHWIFE"
msgstr "Fishwife"

msgid "NPC_DOCK_SENTINEL"
msgstr "Dock Watchman"

msgid "VALUABLE_SHIP_HELM"
msgstr "Living Hull's Helm"

msgid "VALUABLE_GOLDEN_SHARK_TOOTH"
msgstr "Shark's Golden Tooth"

msgid "VALUABLE_KEY_ANCHOR"
msgstr "Anchor Key"

msgid "VALUABLE_KEY_COMPASS"
msgstr "Compass Key"

msgid "TOAST_HULL_AWAKENS"
msgstr "The hull creaks and rises: the Living Hull awakens!"

msgid "TOAST_SHARK_AWAKENS"
msgstr "The water boils: the Pork Shark leaps onto the pier!"

msgid "QUEST_DOCK_HELM"
msgstr "The Lost Helm"

msgid "QUEST_DOCK_HELM_DESC"
msgstr "The Harbor Master wants his helm back: a beached hull in the Shipyard (west of the market) wakes as the Living Hull, which carries it. Touch the hull, defeat it and bring the helm: in return you get the Anchor Key, one of the two for the Drowned Captain's gate."

msgid "QUEST_DOCK_TOOTH"
msgstr "The Golden Tooth"

msgid "QUEST_DOCK_TOOTH_DESC"
msgstr "The Fishwife lost her husband's golden tooth to the Pork Shark, at the Fishery east of the market. Her words wake it; defeat it and bring the tooth to receive the Compass Key, the other one for the Drowned Captain's gate."

msgid "QUEST_DOCK_GATE"
msgstr "The Captain's Gate"

msgid "QUEST_DOCK_GATE_DESC"
msgstr "The Dock Watchman only opens the gate for those with both keys: the Anchor (Harbor Master) and the Compass (Fishwife). Beyond lies the Drowned Captain's Deck."

msgid "DLG_DOCKMASTER_1"
msgstr "Low tide, strangers, and still the port does not sleep. I have run this dock for thirty years and never seen the sea so restless."

msgid "DLG_DOCKMASTER_2"
msgstr "A beached hull in the Shipyard, west of the market, moves at night. It swallowed the helm of my last ship, and without it I cannot cast off anything here."

msgid "DLG_DOCKMASTER_3"
msgstr "Touch the hull, bring down what comes out and bring me the helm. In return I give the Anchor Key, one of the two that open the Drowned Captain's gate at the end of the dock."

msgid "DLG_DOCKMASTER_ACTIVE"
msgstr "The Shipyard is west of the fish market: follow the main pier and turn left. The helm is bronze and smells of salt. Bring it and the key is yours."

msgid "DLG_DOCKMASTER_DONE"
msgstr "My helm! Now this old port has a future again. The Anchor Key is yours; take it to the Watchman, together with the Compass one."

msgid "DLG_HULL_1"
msgstr "The planks are warm and damp, and new nails sprout from the wood. Something large breathes inside the hull."

msgid "DLG_HULL_2"
msgstr "The Living Hull awakens!"

msgid "DLG_HULL_LOCKED"
msgstr "An old hull on its cradle. Nothing answers your hands."

msgid "DLG_FISHWIFE_1"
msgstr "Fresh fish, today only! ...Oh, sorry, habit. Today I have nothing to sell: the Pork Shark has been eating all the nets."

msgid "DLG_FISHWIFE_2"
msgstr "It also took my husband's golden tooth, which fell in the water when he fought the beast. It was all we had of value."

msgid "DLG_FISHWIFE_3"
msgstr "I will call the beast for you, here at the Fishery. Bring down the Pork Shark and bring the tooth: I give the Compass Key, the other for the Drowned Captain's gate."

msgid "DLG_FISHWIFE_ACTIVE"
msgstr "The tooth shines brighter than a fresh scale. It is in the beast's mouth. Bring it down and bring the tooth to me."

msgid "DLG_FISHWIFE_DONE"
msgstr "My old man's tooth! The Compass Key is yours. Take it to the Watchman, in the lane north of the wharf."

msgid "DLG_FISHWIFE_WAIT"
msgstr "The nets are torn, but the tide returns. Take a fish, it is fresh."

msgid "DLG_DOCKGUARD_1"
msgstr "Stop there. This gate closes the Deck, and on the Deck the Drowned Captain rules. He sailed to the bottom of the sea and came back with his whole crew."

msgid "DLG_DOCKGUARD_2"
msgstr "The gate only opens with TWO keys: the Anchor and the Compass. The first is with the Harbor Master at the landing; the second, with the Fishwife at the Fishery."

msgid "DLG_DOCKGUARD_3"
msgstr "Each charges a price: a helm, a golden tooth. Bring both keys to me and I will open the way."

msgid "DLG_DOCKGUARD_ACTIVE"
msgstr "I only open with both keys, Anchor and Compass, in the same bag. The Harbor Master is at the landing; the Fishwife, at the Fishery east of the market."

msgid "DLG_DOCKGUARD_DONE"
msgstr "Both keys! The gate is open. Beware: the Drowned Captain never lost a ship, and he will not lose this one."

msgid "MONSTER_WAR_CHAMPION"
msgstr "Fallen Champion"

msgid "MONSTER_FALLEN_KING"
msgstr "Fallen King"

msgid "NPC_RUINS_SCHOLAR"
msgstr "Ruins Scholar"

msgid "NPC_RUINS_KNIGHT_STATUE"
msgstr "Stone Knight"

msgid "NPC_RUINS_PRIESTESS"
msgstr "Priestess"

msgid "NPC_RUINS_GATEKEEPER"
msgstr "Ruins Gatekeeper"

msgid "VALUABLE_STONE_HEART"
msgstr "Stone Heart"

msgid "VALUABLE_CHAMPION_BANNER"
msgstr "Champion's Banner"

msgid "VALUABLE_KEY_LION"
msgstr "Lion Key"

msgid "VALUABLE_KEY_EAGLE"
msgstr "Eagle Key"

msgid "TOAST_CHAMPION_AWAKENS"
msgstr "The monoliths shake: the Fallen Champion rises!"

msgid "QUEST_RUINS_SEAL"
msgstr "The Stone Heart"

msgid "QUEST_RUINS_SEAL_DESC"
msgstr "The Ruins Scholar, in the Forum just past the entrance, says the stone knight of the Knights' Plaza (west, past the Old Quarter) guards a stone heart. Touch the statue with the quest active, defeat the Ruins Guardian and bring the heart: in return you get the Lion Key, one of the two for the Fallen King's gate."

msgid "QUEST_RUINS_BANNER"
msgstr "The Champion's Banner"

msgid "QUEST_RUINS_BANNER_DESC"
msgstr "The Priestess, in the Monoliths' Plaza (east, past the Market Quarter), wants the banner of the champion who died in the war. Her words wake the Fallen Champion; defeat him and bring the banner to receive the Eagle Key, the other one for the Fallen King's gate."

msgid "QUEST_RUINS_GATE"
msgstr "The King's Gate"

msgid "QUEST_RUINS_GATE_DESC"
msgstr "The Ruins Gatekeeper, in the lane past the Citadel, only opens the gate for those with both keys: the Lion (Scholar) and the Eagle (Priestess). Beyond lies the Fallen King's Royal Vault."

msgid "DLG_SCHOLAR_1"
msgstr "Mind your step: every stone here was once a house wall. I have catalogued these ruins since before the war and only now understand what the king hid."

msgid "DLG_SCHOLAR_2"
msgstr "In the Knights' Plaza, to the west, stands a stone knight with a stone heart in his chest. He sleeps, but obeys whoever touches him with the right intent."

msgid "DLG_SCHOLAR_3"
msgstr "Touch the statue, bring down the Guardian and bring me the heart. In return I give the Lion Key, one of the two that open the Fallen King's gate, north of the Citadel."

msgid "DLG_SCHOLAR_ACTIVE"
msgstr "The Knights' Plaza is west of the Forum: cross the Old Quarter, where the streets became a maze, and go north. The heart is grey and heavy as lead."

msgid "DLG_SCHOLAR_DONE"
msgstr "The heart! At last I can close this chapter of my catalogue. The Lion Key is yours; take it to the Gatekeeper, together with the Eagle one."

msgid "DLG_KNIGHT_STATUE_1"
msgstr "The stone is warm under your hand, and something beats inside, slowly, like an enormous heart."

msgid "DLG_KNIGHT_STATUE_2"
msgstr "The Ruins Guardian awakens!"

msgid "DLG_KNIGHT_STATUE_LOCKED"
msgstr "A stone knight, motionless, sword lowered. Nothing answers your touch."

msgid "DLG_PRIESTESS_1"
msgstr "I light candles for those left without a grave. Here, among the monoliths, the greatest champion of the war fell, and his banner was never buried with him."

msgid "DLG_PRIESTESS_2"
msgstr "But he does not rest: each moon he rises, searching for the banner, and breaks whatever he finds. Only a blade convinces him to lie down again."

msgid "DLG_PRIESTESS_3"
msgstr "I will call him for you, here in the plaza. Bring down the Fallen Champion and bring the banner: I give the Eagle Key, the other for the Fallen King's gate."

msgid "DLG_PRIESTESS_ACTIVE"
msgstr "The banner is red and torn, and he clasps it to his chest. Bring him down with respect and bring the cloth to me."

msgid "DLG_PRIESTESS_DONE"
msgstr "The banner! Now he can rest. The Eagle Key is yours. Take it to the Gatekeeper, at the lane north of the Citadel."

msgid "DLG_PRIESTESS_WAIT"
msgstr "The candles still burn. Go in peace, and return if you need a blessing."

msgid "DLG_RGUARD_1"
msgstr "Halt. This gate closes the Royal Vault, and in the Vault the Fallen King rules. He died defending the treasure and refused to leave it."

msgid "DLG_RGUARD_2"
msgstr "The gate only opens with TWO keys: the Lion and the Eagle. The first is with the Scholar, in the Forum; the second, with the Priestess, in the Monoliths' Plaza."

msgid "DLG_RGUARD_3"
msgstr "Each charges a price: a stone heart, an old banner. Bring both keys to me and I will open the way."

msgid "DLG_RGUARD_ACTIVE"
msgstr "I only open with both keys, Lion and Eagle, in the same bag. The Scholar is in the Forum; the Priestess, in the Monoliths' Plaza, to the east."

msgid "DLG_RGUARD_DONE"
msgstr "Both keys! The gate is open. Beware: the Fallen King never lost a duel, and not even death took his crown."

msgid "MONSTER_FORT_BARON"
msgstr "Infernal Baron"

msgid "NPC_FORT_SERGEANT"
msgstr "Garrison Sergeant"

msgid "NPC_FORT_GATEKEEPER"
msgstr "Fort Jailer"

msgid "VALUABLE_DARK_BLADE"
msgstr "Elf Lord's Blade"

msgid "VALUABLE_QUEEN_RING"
msgstr "Queen's Ring"

msgid "VALUABLE_KEY_RUBY"
msgstr "Ruby Key"

msgid "VALUABLE_KEY_ONYX"
msgstr "Onyx Key"

msgid "QUEST_FORT_PURGE"
msgstr "Clear the Barracks"

msgid "QUEST_FORT_PURGE_DESC"
msgstr "The Garrison Sergeant asks that both barracks, West and East (just past the Armory Yard), be cleared of the cursed soldiers still holding them."

msgid "QUEST_FORT_SIGIL"
msgstr "The Elf Lord's Blade"

msgid "QUEST_FORT_SIGIL_DESC"
msgstr "The Exile, in the Ossuary to the west, wants back the blade the Dark Elf Lord took from him. His words wake the Dark Elf Lord; defeat him and bring the blade: in return you get the Onyx Key, one of the two for the Baron's gate."

msgid "QUEST_FORT_RING"
msgstr "The Queen's Ring"

msgid "QUEST_FORT_RING_DESC"
msgstr "The Penitent, in the Throne Hall to the east, swore to return the ring the Succubus Queen wears. Her words wake the Queen; defeat her and bring the ring to receive the Ruby Key, the other one for the Baron's gate."

msgid "QUEST_FORT_GATE"
msgstr "The Baron's Gate"

msgid "QUEST_FORT_GATE_DESC"
msgstr "The Fort Jailer, in the lane north of the Gallery, only opens the gate for those with both keys: the Onyx (Exile) and the Ruby (Penitent). Beyond lies the Infernal Baron's Hall."

msgid "DLG_FSERGEANT_1"
msgstr "Welcome to the Garrison. This is where the kingdom watched the south, until the Baron opened the doors below and the whole garrison rose again, eyes empty."

msgid "DLG_FSERGEANT_2"
msgstr "The two barracks, West and East, lie past the Armory Yard, and are still full of them. Until they are cleared, nothing gets through the northern routes."

msgid "DLG_FSERGEANT_3"
msgstr "Clear both and I will pay for the work. After that, the Exile and the Penitent have scores to settle, each in a corner of the fort, and they keep the keys to the Baron's gate."

msgid "DLG_FSERGEANT_ACTIVE"
msgstr "The barracks are west and east of the Armory Yard, behind the arched gates. Listen for the footsteps before you open the door."

msgid "DLG_FSERGEANT_DONE"
msgstr "The barracks are calm for the first time in years. Go west or east: the Gallery awaits you up there."

msgid "DLG_FEXILE_1"
msgstr "A fallen knight, that is what I am. I served the Baron until he cast me out for refusing the order to burn the village. Now I live among the Ossuary's coffins, like the rest of the forgotten."

msgid "DLG_FEXILE_2"
msgstr "The Dark Elf Lord, captain of the crossbowmen, took my blade the night I was cast out. He keeps it here at the back of the Ossuary as a trophy, and sleeps with his eyes open."

msgid "DLG_FEXILE_3"
msgstr "I will call him for you. Bring him down and bring the blade: I give the Onyx Key, one of the two that open the Baron's gate, in the lane north of the Gallery."

msgid "DLG_FEXILE_ACTIVE"
msgstr "The blade is long and dark, with a bone hilt. He carries it on his back. Bring him down and I will know it from afar."

msgid "DLG_FEXILE_DONE"
msgstr "My blade! At last I can die as a knight. The Onyx Key is yours: take it to the Jailer, together with the Ruby one."

msgid "DLG_FEXILE_WAIT"
msgstr "The coffins are quiet today. Come back when you need a story."

msgid "DLG_FPENITENT_1"
msgstr "I pray here every day, before the empty throne. I was a lady of the Succubus Queen's court, and I helped seduce half the kingdom for the Baron. Today I carry that weight."

msgid "DLG_FPENITENT_2"
msgstr "The Queen wears a ring that was mine, a ruby ring, a gift from my mother. While it is on her finger, I cannot forgive myself. She sleeps at the back of the hall, and dreams of power."

msgid "DLG_FPENITENT_3"
msgstr "I will wake her for you. Bring down the Queen and bring the ring: I give the Ruby Key, the other for the Baron's gate."

msgid "DLG_FPENITENT_ACTIVE"
msgstr "The ring is small and shines like fresh blood. She clasps it to her chest. Bring her down carefully: she sings before she strikes."

msgid "DLG_FPENITENT_DONE"
msgstr "My mother's ring! Perhaps now I can pray in peace. The Ruby Key is yours: take it to the Jailer, together with the Onyx one."

msgid "DLG_FPENITENT_WAIT"
msgstr "The throne is still empty, but the candles still burn. Go in peace."

msgid "DLG_FGUARD_1"
msgstr "Halt. This gate closes the Baron's Hall, and in the Hall the Infernal Baron rules. I was his jailer so long I forgot what daylight was."

msgid "DLG_FGUARD_2"
msgstr "The gate only opens with TWO keys: the Onyx and the Ruby. The first is with the Exile, in the Ossuary to the west; the second, with the Penitent, in the Throne Hall to the east."

msgid "DLG_FGUARD_3"
msgstr "Each charges a price: a blade, a ring. Bring both keys to me and I will open the way."

msgid "DLG_FGUARD_ACTIVE"
msgstr "I only open with both keys, Onyx and Ruby, in the same bag. The Exile is to the west, in the Ossuary; the Penitent, to the east, in the Throne Hall."

msgid "DLG_FGUARD_DONE"
msgstr "Both keys! The gate is open. Beware: the Infernal Baron does not receive visitors, and those he does never return."

msgid "ARENA_CATACOMBS"
msgstr "Catacombs"

msgid "PROP_TO_CATACOMBS"
msgstr "Path to the Catacombs"

msgid "MONSTER_CT_HEADSMAN"
msgstr "Catacomb Headsman"

msgid "MONSTER_CT_SOUL"
msgstr "Chained Soul"

msgid "MONSTER_CT_KING"
msgstr "Chained King"

msgid "NPC_CT_MONK"
msgstr "Catacomb Friar"

msgid "NPC_CT_JAILER"
msgstr "Blind Jailer"

msgid "NPC_CT_GIBBET"
msgstr "Headsman's Gibbet"

msgid "NPC_CT_PRISONER"
msgstr "Prisoner"

msgid "NPC_CT_WARDEN"
msgstr "Catacomb Warden"

msgid "VALUABLE_HEADSMAN_AXE"
msgstr "Headsman's Axe"

msgid "VALUABLE_SOUL_SHACKLE"
msgstr "Soul Shackle"

msgid "VALUABLE_KEY_IRON"
msgstr "Iron Key"

msgid "VALUABLE_KEY_BONE"
msgstr "Bone Key"

msgid "TOAST_GIBBET_AWAKENS"
msgstr "The gibbet creaks and its chains fall loose: the Headsman drops into the Pit!"

msgid "TOAST_SOUL_AWAKENS"
msgstr "The shackles snap: the Chained Soul breaks free!"

msgid "QUEST_CT_PURGE"
msgstr "Clear the Cells"

msgid "QUEST_CT_PURGE_DESC"
msgstr "The Catacomb Friar asks that both Cell Wings, west and east of the Nave of Bones, be cleared of the dead who still guard the prisoners."

msgid "QUEST_CT_AXE"
msgstr "The Headsman's Axe"

msgid "QUEST_CT_AXE_DESC"
msgstr "The Blind Jailer, in the Nave of Bones, wants the Headsman's axe to settle his accounts. Touch the gibbet in the Headsman's Pit (west, past the Torture Room) with the quest active to wake the Catacomb Headsman; defeat him and bring the axe: in return you get the Iron Key, one of the two for the Chained King's gate."

msgid "QUEST_CT_SOUL"
msgstr "The Soul Shackle"

msgid "QUEST_CT_SOUL_DESC"
msgstr "The Prisoner, in the Chapel of the Chained (east, past the Ossuary), has been held for centuries by a shackle that also binds a soul. Her words wake the Chained Soul; defeat it and bring the shackle to receive the Bone Key, the other one for the Chained King's gate."

msgid "QUEST_CT_GATE"
msgstr "The Chained King's Gate"

msgid "QUEST_CT_GATE_DESC"
msgstr "The Catacomb Warden, in the lane north of the Gallery of the Condemned, only opens the gate for those with both keys: the Iron (Blind Jailer) and the Bone (Prisoner). Beyond lies the Chained King's Crypt."

msgid "DLG_CTMONK_1"
msgstr "Peace be with you, even down here. I pray for the prisoners of the Catacombs, who died behind bars without ever being tried."

msgid "DLG_CTMONK_2"
msgstr "Both Cell Wings, west and east of the Nave of Bones, are still full of the dead on guard. They let no soul pass in peace."

msgid "DLG_CTMONK_3"
msgstr "Clear both and I will pay for the work. After that, the Blind Jailer and the Prisoner have scores to settle, and they keep the keys to the King's gate."

msgid "DLG_CTMONK_ACTIVE"
msgstr "The Cell Wings lie left and right of the Nave of Bones. Listen for the chains: where they drag, a dead guard stands."

msgid "DLG_CTMONK_DONE"
msgstr "The cells are silent for the first time in centuries. Go on: the Gallery of the Condemned awaits you."

msgid "DLG_CTJAILER_1"
msgstr "I have not seen since the day the King took my eyes, but I know every cell by heart. I was jailer of these Catacombs for forty years, and the Headsman was my only friend."

msgid "DLG_CTJAILER_2"
msgstr "He died in the Pit, to the west, past the Torture Room, and came back hanging in a gibbet, axe on his back, still wanting work. That is no life for a friend."

msgid "DLG_CTJAILER_3"
msgstr "Touch the gibbet, bring down the Headsman and bring me the axe. In return I give the Iron Key, one of the two that open the Chained King's gate, in the lane north of the Gallery."

msgid "DLG_CTJAILER_ACTIVE"
msgstr "The Headsman's Pit is to the west: go through the Cell Wing and the Torture Room. The axe is heavy and has a bone handle. I know it by the smell."

msgid "DLG_CTJAILER_DONE"
msgstr "My friend's axe! Now he can rest. The Iron Key is yours: take it to the Warden, together with the Bone one."

msgid "DLG_CTGIBBET_1"
msgstr "The gibbet sways without wind, and the chains chime as if someone breathed inside. Something huge stirs among the bones."

msgid "DLG_CTGIBBET_2"
msgstr "The Catacomb Headsman descends!"

msgid "DLG_CTGIBBET_LOCKED"
msgstr "An iron gibbet hanging from a beam, creaking. Nothing answers your touch."

msgid "DLG_CTPRISONER_1"
msgstr "I have been here since before you were born, chained to this altar. They say I stole from the King; I never stole anything. I only saw what I should not have."

msgid "DLG_CTPRISONER_2"
msgstr "The shackle on my wrist also binds a soul, that of the guard who watched me and died of guilt. It drags itself through the Chapel and will not let me sleep."

msgid "DLG_CTPRISONER_3"
msgstr "I will free it for you, here in the Chapel. Bring down the Chained Soul and bring the shackle: I give the Bone Key, the other for the Chained King's gate."

msgid "DLG_CTPRISONER_ACTIVE"
msgstr "The shackle is cold iron and glows blue when the soul is near. Bring it down carefully: it weeps before it strikes."

msgid "DLG_CTPRISONER_DONE"
msgstr "I am free! After so many years... The Bone Key is yours: take it to the Warden, together with the Iron one."

msgid "DLG_CTPRISONER_WAIT"
msgstr "The chains still chime, but they no longer weigh on me. Go in peace."

msgid "DLG_CTWARDEN_1"
msgstr "Halt. This gate closes the Crypt, and in the Crypt the Chained King serves the sentence the kingdom owes him. I am the last who visits him."

msgid "DLG_CTWARDEN_2"
msgstr "The gate only opens with TWO keys: the Iron and the Bone. The first is with the Blind Jailer in the Nave of Bones; the second, with the Prisoner in the Chapel of the Chained, to the east."

msgid "DLG_CTWARDEN_3"
msgstr "Each charges a price: an axe, a shackle. Bring both keys to me and I will open the way."

msgid "DLG_CTWARDEN_ACTIVE"
msgstr "I only open with both keys, Iron and Bone, in the same bag. The Blind Jailer is in the Nave of Bones; the Prisoner, in the Chapel, to the east."

msgid "DLG_CTWARDEN_DONE"
msgstr "Both keys! The gate is open. Beware: the Chained King has broken every chain that held him, except the one of shame."

msgid "MONSTER_MN_QUARTZ_BEAST"
msgstr "Quartz Beast"

msgid "NPC_MN_APPRENTICE"
msgstr "Mining Apprentice"

msgid "NPC_MN_FOREMAN"
msgstr "Foreman Brokk"

msgid "NPC_MN_ORE_CART"
msgstr "Abandoned Ore Cart"

msgid "NPC_MN_JEWELER"
msgstr "Jeweler Dolgrim"

msgid "NPC_MN_CRYSTAL"
msgstr "Pulsing Crystal"

msgid "NPC_MN_GATEKEEPER"
msgstr "Keywarden Thrain"

msgid "VALUABLE_TROLL_TUSK"
msgstr "Troll Chief's Tusk"

msgid "VALUABLE_QUARTZ_CORE"
msgstr "Quartz Core"

msgid "VALUABLE_KEY_PICKAXE"
msgstr "Pickaxe Key"

msgid "VALUABLE_KEY_LANTERN"
msgstr "Lantern Key"

msgid "TOAST_ORE_CART_AWAKENS"
msgstr "The cart shakes on its rails: the Troll Chief awakens!"

msgid "TOAST_CRYSTAL_AWAKENS"
msgstr "The crystal pulses and cracks: the Quartz Beast breaks free!"

msgid "QUEST_MN_CLEAR"
msgstr "Clear the Galleries"

msgid "QUEST_MN_CLEAR_DESC"
msgstr "The Mining Apprentice, at the entrance, asks that the first two packs holding the galleries near the rails be brought down, so the crew can work."

msgid "QUEST_MN_TUSK"
msgstr "The Troll Chief's Tusk"

msgid "QUEST_MN_TUSK_DESC"
msgstr "Foreman Brokk, at the Dwarves' Camp (east, near the entrance), wants the tusk of the Troll Chief, who sleeps in an abandoned ore cart in the Cart Cave (west). Touch the cart with the quest active, defeat the Troll Chief and bring the tusk: in return you get the Pickaxe Key, one of the two for the Mine Heart's gate."

msgid "QUEST_MN_QUARTZ"
msgstr "The Quartz Core"

msgid "QUEST_MN_QUARTZ_DESC"
msgstr "Jeweler Dolgrim, in the Jeweler's House (west, high in the maze), wants the quartz core the Quartz Beast guards in the Crystal Hall (east). Touch the Pulsing Crystal with the quest active, defeat the beast and bring the core to receive the Lantern Key, the other one for the Mine Heart's gate."

msgid "QUEST_MN_GATE"
msgstr "The Mine Heart's Gate"

msgid "QUEST_MN_GATE_DESC"
msgstr "Keywarden Thrain, in the tunnel north of the maze (follow the rails), only opens the gate for those with both keys: the Pickaxe (Foreman) and the Lantern (Jeweler). Beyond lies the Mine Heart, where the Crystal Golem waits."

msgid "DLG_MNAPP_1"
msgstr "Ah, visitors! Mind the rails: they are the only safe way in this mine. Off them the maze closes in, and I have lost three pickaxes and an uncle in it."

msgid "DLG_MNAPP_2"
msgstr "The first two packs, right here, took the front galleries. Without them clear, the crew cannot haul the carts."

msgid "DLG_MNAPP_3"
msgstr "Bring both down and I will pay. Then talk to Foreman Brokk, at the camp to the east: he knows how to open the Mine Heart's gate."

msgid "DLG_MNAPP_ACTIVE"
msgstr "The front galleries are beside the rails. The packs make noise: you can hear them from afar."

msgid "DLG_MNAPP_DONE"
msgstr "What a relief! Now the crew goes back to work. Follow the rails north, and do not leave them without a lantern."

msgid "DLG_MNFORE_1"
msgstr "Brokk, foreman of this mine for forty years. The Heart's gate only opens with two keys, and one of them is held by a troll sleeping in an old cart, in the Cart Cave, far to the west."

msgid "DLG_MNFORE_2"
msgstr "He stole an ivory tusk I used as a lucky charm, and since then the mine has given only misfortune. The tusk is stuck in his mouth, the beast."

msgid "DLG_MNFORE_3"
msgstr "Touch the cart, bring down the Troll Chief and bring the tusk. I give the Pickaxe Key. Follow the rails to the Cave: they lead there."

msgid "DLG_MNFORE_ACTIVE"
msgstr "The Cart Cave is to the west, on a branch of the rails. The tusk is yellowed and as long as your arm. Bring it and the key is yours."

msgid "DLG_MNFORE_DONE"
msgstr "My tusk! Luck returns to the mine. The Pickaxe Key is yours: take it to the Keywarden, in the tunnel to the north, together with the Lantern one."

msgid "DLG_MNCART_1"
msgstr "The cart's wood is cold, but the iron of the rails hums, as if something huge breathed under the ore."

msgid "DLG_MNCART_2"
msgstr "The Troll Chief awakens!"

msgid "DLG_MNCART_LOCKED"
msgstr "An abandoned ore cart on the rails. Nothing answers your touch."

msgid "DLG_MNJEW_1"
msgstr "Thirty years cutting this mine's stones, and the finest never reached my hands: the Quartz Core, the heart of the giant crystal in the Crystal Hall, to the east."

msgid "DLG_MNJEW_2"
msgstr "The crystal pulses like a living heart, and from it was born a quartz beast that guards it. It only wakes when someone touches the Pulsing Crystal with ill intent."

msgid "DLG_MNJEW_3"
msgstr "Touch the crystal, bring down the Quartz Beast and bring me the core. In return I give the Lantern Key, the other one that opens the Mine Heart's gate."

msgid "DLG_MNJEW_ACTIVE"
msgstr "The Crystal Hall is to the east, on a branch of the rails, after many turns. The core glows blue and is warm to the touch. Bring it to me."

msgid "DLG_MNJEW_DONE"
msgstr "The core! It is even lovelier than I dreamed. The Lantern Key is yours: take it to the Keywarden, together with the Pickaxe one."

msgid "DLG_MNJEW_WAIT"
msgstr "Every stone has a story. Come back when you want to hear one."

msgid "DLG_MNCRY_1"
msgstr "The crystal pulses, warm, in purple, and thin cracks run inside it. Something moves deep within."

msgid "DLG_MNCRY_2"
msgstr "The Quartz Beast breaks free!"

msgid "DLG_MNCRY_LOCKED"
msgstr "A purple crystal, motionless, glowing softly. Nothing answers your touch."

msgid "DLG_MNGUARD_1"
msgstr "Halt. This gate closes the Mine Heart, and in the Heart lives the Crystal Golem, born of all the ore we tore out. I have kept the keys longer than the gate has had rust."

msgid "DLG_MNGUARD_2"
msgstr "The gate only opens with TWO keys: the Pickaxe and the Lantern. The first is with Foreman Brokk, at the camp to the east; the second, with Jeweler Dolgrim, in his house to the west."

msgid "DLG_MNGUARD_3"
msgstr "Each charges a price: a tusk, a crystal core. Bring both keys to me and I will open the way."

msgid "DLG_MNGUARD_ACTIVE"
msgstr "I only open with both keys, Pickaxe and Lantern, in the same bag. The Foreman is to the east; the Jeweler, to the west. Follow the rails."

msgid "DLG_MNGUARD_DONE"
msgstr "Both keys! The gate is open. Beware: the Crystal Golem feels no pain, and every piece that falls from him becomes a blade."

msgid "MONSTER_BK_ARMOR"
msgstr "Living Armor"

msgid "MONSTER_BK_COMMANDER"
msgstr "Rotting Commander"

msgid "MONSTER_BK_GENERAL"
msgstr "General Rust"

msgid "NPC_BK_SERGEANT"
msgstr "Garrison Sergeant"

msgid "NPC_BK_QUARTERMASTER"
msgstr "Quartermaster Vorn"

msgid "NPC_BK_RACK"
msgstr "Weapon Rack"

msgid "NPC_BK_MEDIC"
msgstr "Field Medic Lena"

msgid "NPC_BK_COT"
msgstr "Commander's Cot"

msgid "NPC_BK_GATEKEEPER"
msgstr "Gate Sentinel"

msgid "VALUABLE_ARMORY_SEAL"
msgstr "Armory Seal"

msgid "VALUABLE_KEY_BRASS"
msgstr "Brass Key"

msgid "VALUABLE_KEY_STEEL"
msgstr "Steel Key"

msgid "TOAST_ARMORY_AWAKENS"
msgstr "The weapons clatter on their racks: the Living Armor rises!"

msgid "TOAST_COT_AWAKENS"
msgstr "The cot creaks: the Rotting Commander rises!"

msgid "QUEST_BK_CLEAR"
msgstr "Clear the Entrance"

msgid "QUEST_BK_CLEAR_DESC"
msgstr "The Garrison Sergeant asks that the first two packs roaming the rooms near the entrance be brought down before the army of shadows organizes."

msgid "QUEST_BK_SEAL"
msgstr "The Armory Seal"

msgid "QUEST_BK_SEAL_DESC"
msgstr "Quartermaster Vorn, in the Supply Depot (east, near the entrance), lost the seal that locked the Armory: a suit of war armor carries it. Touch the weapon rack in the Armory (west) with the quest active, defeat the Living Armor and bring the seal: in return you get the Brass Key, one of the two for General Rust's gate."

msgid "QUEST_BK_MEDAL"
msgstr "The War Medal"

msgid "QUEST_BK_MEDAL_DESC"
msgstr "Field Medic Lena, in the Infirmary (west, high up), wants the war medal of the commander who died in the Barracks (east). Touch his cot with the quest active, defeat the Rotting Commander and bring the medal to receive the Steel Key, the other one for General Rust's gate."

msgid "QUEST_BK_GATE"
msgstr "The Command Room Gate"

msgid "QUEST_BK_GATE_DESC"
msgstr "The Gate Sentinel, in the tunnel north of the maze, only opens the gate for those with both keys: the Brass (Quartermaster) and the Steel (Medic). Beyond lies General Rust's Command Room."

msgid "DLG_BKSGT_1"
msgstr "Halt, civilians. This bunker was the king's army's last trench, and it is still full of weapons, tools and food. It is also full of the soldiers who never left."

msgid "DLG_BKSGT_2"
msgstr "The rooms near the entrance are filling up again. Two packs, the closest ones, before the rest wake."

msgid "DLG_BKSGT_3"
msgstr "Bring both down and I will pay. Then look for Quartermaster Vorn, at the depot to the east: he and Medic Lena keep the keys to the General's gate."

msgid "DLG_BKSGT_ACTIVE"
msgstr "The rooms lie just past the garrison, behind the wide gaps. Listen for footsteps before entering."

msgid "DLG_BKSGT_DONE"
msgstr "Good work. The way is yours now: the bunker is a maze, so follow the walls and note what you pass."

msgid "DLG_BKQM_1"
msgstr "Vorn, quartermaster, thirty years counting every crate in this depot. One seal is missing: the Armory's, the wax seal that proves the weapons are the king's."

msgid "DLG_BKQM_2"
msgstr "A suit of war armor took it: it stands in the Armory, to the west, among the racks, and wakes if anyone touches the weapons. It was the last to leave armed."

msgid "DLG_BKQM_3"
msgstr "Touch the rack, bring down the Living Armor and bring me the seal. I give the Brass Key, one of the two that open the General's gate, in the tunnel to the north."

msgid "DLG_BKQM_ACTIVE"
msgstr "The Armory is to the west: cross the maze to the room of racks. The seal is red wax, stuck to the breastplate. Bring it."

msgid "DLG_BKQM_DONE"
msgstr "The Armory seal! Now the books balance. The Brass Key is yours: take it to the Sentinel, together with the Steel one."

msgid "DLG_BKRACK_1"
msgstr "The weapons hum on the racks, shields knock against each other, and an iron shadow moves among the spears."

msgid "DLG_BKRACK_2"
msgstr "The Living Armor rises!"

msgid "DLG_BKRACK_LOCKED"
msgstr "An old weapon rack with spears and shields. Nothing answers your touch."

msgid "DLG_BKMED_1"
msgstr "I tended the wounded here until the last day. The commander died in the Barracks, to the east, with his war medal on his chest, and never let me bury him."

msgid "DLG_BKMED_2"
msgstr "He does not rest: he rises from the cot and wanders the barracks, looking for someone to give orders to. Only a fight convinces him to lie down again."

msgid "DLG_BKMED_3"
msgstr "Touch his cot, bring down the Rotting Commander and bring the medal. I give the Steel Key, the other for General Rust's gate."

msgid "DLG_BKMED_ACTIVE"
msgstr "The Barracks lie to the east, with rows of cots. The medal is bronze, with an eagle. Bring it to me."

msgid "DLG_BKMED_DONE"
msgstr "His medal! Now I can bury him with honor. The Steel Key is yours: take it to the Sentinel, together with the Brass one."

msgid "DLG_BKMED_WAIT"
msgstr "The beds are clean and the bandages dry. Come back if you need healing."

msgid "DLG_BKCOT_1"
msgstr "The mattress is still warm, and the medal gleams on the pillow where a chest no longer breathes."

msgid "DLG_BKCOT_2"
msgstr "The Rotting Commander rises!"

msgid "DLG_BKCOT_LOCKED"
msgstr "A military cot, empty and cold. Nothing answers your touch."

msgid "DLG_BKGUARD_1"
msgstr "Halt. This gate closes the Command Room, and in the Room General Rust rules, who never accepted surrender and had the bunker sealed with everyone inside."

msgid "DLG_BKGUARD_2"
msgstr "The gate only opens with TWO keys: the Brass and the Steel. The first is with Quartermaster Vorn, in the depot to the east; the second, with Medic Lena, in the infirmary to the west."

msgid "DLG_BKGUARD_3"
msgstr "Each charges a price: a seal, a medal. Bring both keys to me and I will open the way."

msgid "DLG_BKGUARD_ACTIVE"
msgstr "I only open with both keys, Brass and Steel, in the same bag. The Quartermaster is to the east; the Medic, to the west."

msgid "DLG_BKGUARD_DONE"
msgstr "Both keys! The gate is open. Beware: General Rust accepts no visitors, and his rust eats even steel."

msgid "VALUABLE_COMMANDER_MEDAL"
msgstr "Commander's Medal"

msgid "MONSTER_FD_VIPER"
msgstr "Ancient Viper"

msgid "MONSTER_FD_SPORE_KING"
msgstr "Spore King"

msgid "MONSTER_FD_ELDER"
msgstr "Shadow Elder"

msgid "NPC_FD_WOODCUTTER"
msgstr "Woodcutter Ardo"

msgid "NPC_FD_HERBALIST"
msgstr "Herbalist Mirta"

msgid "NPC_FD_TOTEM"
msgstr "Serpent Totem"

msgid "NPC_FD_CHARMER"
msgstr "Charmer Zhar"

msgid "NPC_FD_MUSHROOM"
msgstr "Ancestral Mushroom"

msgid "NPC_FD_WARDEN"
msgstr "Forest Warden"

msgid "VALUABLE_VIPER_FANG"
msgstr "Ancient Viper's Fang"

msgid "VALUABLE_SPORE_CROWN"
msgstr "Spore Crown"

msgid "VALUABLE_KEY_MOSS"
msgstr "Moss Key"

msgid "VALUABLE_KEY_THORN"
msgstr "Thorn Key"

msgid "TOAST_TOTEM_AWAKENS"
msgstr "The stones hiss: the Ancient Viper slides down from the totem!"

msgid "TOAST_SPORE_AWAKENS"
msgstr "A cloud of spores rises: the Spore King awakens!"

msgid "QUEST_FD_CLEAR"
msgstr "Clear the Thicket"

msgid "QUEST_FD_CLEAR_DESC"
msgstr "Woodcutter Ardo, in the Edge Glade, asks that the first two packs holding the Thicket just to the north be brought down, so he can chop wood in peace again."

msgid "QUEST_FD_FANG"
msgstr "The Ancient Viper's Fang"

msgid "QUEST_FD_FANG_DESC"
msgstr "Herbalist Mirta, in the Mushroom Grove (east), needs the Ancient Viper's fang to brew the antidote. Touch the Serpent Totem in the Glade (west, past the Snake Bog) with the quest active, defeat the Viper and bring the fang: in return you get the Moss Key, one of the two for the Shadow Elder's gate."

msgid "QUEST_FD_CROWN"
msgstr "The Spore Crown"

msgid "QUEST_FD_CROWN_DESC"
msgstr "Charmer Zhar, in the Snake Bog (west), wants the Spore King's spore crown to calm the snakes. Touching the Ancestral Mushroom in the Spore Circle (east) wakes the King; defeat him and bring the crown to receive the Thorn Key, the other one for the Shadow Elder's gate."

msgid "QUEST_FD_GATE"
msgstr "The Elder's Gate"

msgid "QUEST_FD_GATE_DESC"
msgstr "The Forest Warden, in the lane north of the Bat Grove, only opens the gate for those with both keys: the Moss (Herbalist) and the Thorn (Charmer). Beyond lies the Shadow Elder's Lair."

msgid "DLG_FDWOOD_1"
msgstr "Mind your step: in this wood not even the trees are alive, and what moves between them is worse. I chop wood here at the edge, where one can still breathe."

msgid "DLG_FDWOOD_2"
msgstr "The first two packs, here in the Thicket to the north, have hemmed in my glade. Without them gone I cannot even fetch firewood."

msgid "DLG_FDWOOD_3"
msgstr "Bring both down and I will pay. Then talk to Herbalist Mirta, in the mushroom grove to the east, and to Charmer Zhar, in the bog to the west: they keep the keys to the Elder's gate."

msgid "DLG_FDWOOD_ACTIVE"
msgstr "The Thicket lies just north of the glade. Listen for wings: where there are bats, there is a pack."

msgid "DLG_FDWOOD_DONE"
msgstr "What a good silence! Now choose: west through the snakes, east through the mushrooms or straight north through the dry wood. All paths lead there."

msgid "DLG_FDHERB_1"
msgstr "I have gathered mushrooms and herbs for thirty years and know each by its smell. Today I need only one thing: the Ancient Viper's fang, for the antidote to this forest's poison."

msgid "DLG_FDHERB_2"
msgstr "She lives in the Serpent Glade, to the west, past the bog, coiled around a stone totem. She only wakes if someone touches the totem intending to hunt her."

msgid "DLG_FDHERB_3"
msgstr "Touch the totem, bring down the Viper and bring me the fang. I give the Moss Key, one of the two that open the Shadow Elder's gate, in the lane north of the bat grove."

msgid "DLG_FDHERB_ACTIVE"
msgstr "The Glade is west of the Thicket, past the Snake Bog. The fang is green, curved and the size of a sickle. Bring it."

msgid "DLG_FDHERB_DONE"
msgstr "The fang! Now the antidote can be brewed. The Moss Key is yours: take it to the Warden, together with the Thorn one."

msgid "DLG_FDHERB_WAIT"
msgstr "The mushrooms glow brighter when someone is kind to them. Come back anytime."

msgid "DLG_FDTOTEM_1"
msgstr "The ring of stones hisses softly, and something slides between them, slowly, leaving a trail of scales."

msgid "DLG_FDTOTEM_2"
msgstr "The Ancient Viper slides down from the totem!"

msgid "DLG_FDTOTEM_LOCKED"
msgstr "A moss-covered stone totem. Nothing answers your touch."

msgid "DLG_FDCHARM_1"
msgstr "Shh, do not shout: they hear everything. I charm this bog's snakes with a flute, but lately they do not even listen, stirred up by something in the east."

msgid "DLG_FDCHARM_2"
msgstr "It is the Spore King, in the Spore Circle: his crown sheds a dust that maddens any cold-blooded creature. Without the crown, the snakes calm down."

msgid "DLG_FDCHARM_3"
msgstr "Speak to the Ancestral Mushroom in the circle and the King wakes. Bring him down and bring the crown: I give the Thorn Key, the other for the Elder's gate."

msgid "DLG_FDCHARM_ACTIVE"
msgstr "The Spore Circle is east, past the Mushroom Grove. The crown is purple and gives off smoke. Do not breathe near it."

msgid "DLG_FDCHARM_DONE"
msgstr "The crown! The snakes are listening to me again. The Thorn Key is yours: take it to the Warden, together with the Moss one."

msgid "DLG_FDCHARM_WAIT"
msgstr "The flute plays itself when I am calm. Come back when you wish to hear it."

msgid "DLG_FDMUSH_1"
msgstr "The giant mushroom pulses purple, releasing spores that glow in the air, and a huge cap leans over you as if listening."

msgid "DLG_FDMUSH_2"
msgstr "The Spore King awakens!"

msgid "DLG_FDMUSH_LOCKED"
msgstr "A huge mushroom, motionless, ringed by companions. Nothing answers your touch."

msgid "DLG_FDWARD_1"
msgstr "Halt. This gate closes the Lair, and in the Lair lives the Shadow Elder, a tree already old before this forest darkened. I have tended the gate since it still had leaves."

msgid "DLG_FDWARD_2"
msgstr "The gate only opens with TWO keys: the Moss and the Thorn. The first is with Herbalist Mirta, in the mushroom grove to the east; the second, with Charmer Zhar, in the bog to the west."

msgid "DLG_FDWARD_3"
msgstr "Each charges a price: a fang, a crown. Bring both keys to me and I will open the way."

msgid "DLG_FDWARD_ACTIVE"
msgstr "I only open with both keys, Moss and Thorn, in the same bag. The Herbalist is to the east; the Charmer, to the west."

msgid "DLG_FDWARD_DONE"
msgstr "Both keys! The gate is open. Beware: the Shadow Elder does not run, he does not need to; every root in this forest answers to him."

msgid "MONSTER_DK_DROWNED"
msgstr "Drowned Sailor"

msgid "MONSTER_DK_GATOR"
msgstr "Dock Alligator"

msgid "MONSTER_DK_CRAB"
msgstr "Carrion Crab"

msgid "MONSTER_DK_DECKHAND"
msgstr "Dead Pirate"

msgid "MONSTER_RU_GHOST"
msgstr "Ghost Soldier"

msgid "MONSTER_RU_HOUND"
msgstr "Dead War Hound"

msgid "MONSTER_CE_DIGGER"
msgstr "Mad Gravedigger"

msgid "MONSTER_CE_MAGGOT"
msgstr "Grave Maggot"

msgid "MONSTER_CE_GARGOYLE"
msgstr "Tombstone Gargoyle"

msgid "MONSTER_CE_GHOUL"
msgstr "Bloated Ghoul"

msgid "MONSTER_CE_BRUTE"
msgstr "Gravedigger Ogre"

